<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see warmer weather, snow east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see warmer weather, snow east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Friday were forecast to see warmer weather and snow in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sunny skies and highs of 5.0 to 14 Celsius. Harvest was 85 to 90 percent complete by Monday, Alberta Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should cloudy skies and highs of -7.0 to 3.0 Celsius. Harvest was 94 percent complete by Monday, Saskatchewan Agriculture said.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see some snow and highs of -9.0 to 0.0 Celsius. Manitoba's harvest was virtually complete.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
